═══ CHIP3-en Work has been goin — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: Work has been going badly, is it karma?
Sources: Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: qa_general,qa_metaphysics,introduction
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
That's a heavy feeling to carry — when things keep going wrong at work, it's natural to wonder "why me?" 🙏

From Master Lu's teachings, yes — our career experiences are connected to karma. The conditions we face in this lifetime, including our work environment, relationships with colleagues, and opportunities, are shaped by causes we've set in motion in past and present lives.

But here's what's important: **karma is not a life sentence.** Master Lu taught that we can actively change our karma through sincere practice.

---

A few things that may be happening:

- **Karmic obstacles** — past wrongdoings can create black energy in our field, affecting career, relationships, and health
- **Karmic creditors** — people we've harmed in past lives may be creating friction in our current circumstances
- **A signal to reflect** — sometimes difficulties are an invitation to look inward and change

---

**What you can do right now:**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 7 times daily
*Before reciting:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] with good health and strengthen my spiritual energy"

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 7 times daily
*Before reciting:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] with wisdom and clarity, and remove my worries"
⚠️ Do not recite after 10pm

📿 **Cundi Mantra (准提神咒)** — 21–49 times daily
*Before reciting:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] with smooth progress in my career / help me find a good job"
*(This mantra is specifically for helping wishes come true — career, study, finding work)*

📿 **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** — 1–3 times daily (start with 1)
*Before reciting:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] in repenting and eliminating my karmic obstacles"
⚠️ Do not recite after 10pm

---

Master Lu taught us that learning Buddhism and performing recitations is a **lifelong mission** — not just a short-term fix for current hardships. If we only seek help during difficulties and stop once things improve, we'll be lost again when the next challenge comes.

Keep reciting sincerely. Bodhisattva will help you at the right time 🙏

