═══ CHIP4-en My child is rebell — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: My child is rebellious, how should I handle my emotions?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
That's a really hard place to be in — loving your child deeply while feeling shut out or unheard. 🙏

Here's what Master Lu teaches us about this situation:

**First, understand the root cause**

Master Lu's guidance in the *Metaphysics Q&A* is that when a child is rebellious or conflicts frequently with parents, it may be due to negative karmic ties from previous lives, or the child may have come into the parents' lives to collect karmic debts. Understanding this helps us move from frustration to compassion — this isn't just a personality clash, it's something deeper that can be resolved through practice.

**For your own emotions**

The Heart Sutra is your best friend right now. Reciting it helps *you* gain wisdom, clarity, and calm — so you can respond to your child with patience instead of reacting from pain.

**Recommended daily recitations (for yourself and on behalf of your child):**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3–7 times daily
Prayer: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and strength"

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 7 times or more daily *(not after 10pm)*
Prayer: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless [child's full name] with wisdom, and help them to be cooperative and obedient"

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** — 21 times daily
Prayer: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [child's full name] to resolve our karmic conflicts"

📿 **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** — start with 1 time daily *(not after 10pm)*
Prayer: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], help me to repent and eliminate karmic obstacles"

One important note from Master Lu: reciting the Great Compassion Mantra in large numbers for a rebellious child can actually increase their spiritual power and make them harder to discipline — so keep it to 3–7 times for now.

**The most important thing for your emotions**

Don't try to force change. Master Lu teaches us that each person has their own karma. Your role is to keep your own heart calm, continue your practice, and let Guan Yin Bodhisattva work through the situation in the right timing.

Keep reciting. Your sincere effort is already reaching your child on a level they may not even be aware of. 🙏

Have you been chanting regularly, or is this something new you'd like to start?

═══ CHIP5-en I am new to 心灵法门,  — guard: clean ═══
Q: I am new to 心灵法门, what is the first step?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Welcome! 🙏 It's a beautiful step that you're here.

The Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door, taught by Master Lu Jun Hong, is a practice centered on **Guan Yin Bodhisattva**. The core is simple: through chanting, we purify our mind, reduce karmic obstacles, and gradually transform our life.

---

### Your First Step: Start Chanting These Two

**📿 Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒) — 3 times daily**
Before chanting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health and peace of mind."*

**📿 Heart Sutra (心经) — 3 times daily**
Before chanting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom and remove my worries."*

⚠️ Avoid chanting the Heart Sutra after 10pm.

---

Just these two to start. Consistency matters far more than quantity — even 3 times sincerely every day is a wonderful beginning.

**To learn how to chant (follow-along videos):**
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

---

The practice also has five key methods overall — chanting, making vows, life liberation, repentance, and studying the Dharma in plain language. We can explore those as you get comfortable.

---

